the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=7{a}_{n}-10{a}_{n-1},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,{a}_{2}=21,\\,n\\in N,\\,n\\ge 2\n$$\n\nuse strong induction to prove the following statement:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n},\\,∀n\\in N\n$$\n\n**Base Cases**: We first prove that our statement is true for the base cases $n=$ {{field-1}}.\n\nFor $n=1,$ for the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=2,$ for the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}={{field-5}}\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{{field-6}}={{field-7}}.\n$$\n\nThus, our statement is {{field-8}} for $n=1$ and $n=2.$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that ${a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n}$ for all {{field-9}} for some {{field-10}}. In particular, we have the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{k} & ={{field-11}} \\\\ {a}_{k-1} & ={{field-12}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Inductive Step**: Using the recurrence relation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{k+1} & =({{field-13}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the inductive hypothesis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}_{k}-10{a}_{k-1} & =7({{field-14}})-10({{field-15}}) \\\\  & =5({{field-16}})-2({{field-17}}) \\\\  & ={{field-18}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required.\n\nTherefore, by the principle of strong induction, ${a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n}$ is true for all {{field-19}}." :question/worked-solution "The principle of strong induction states the following: Suppose we have a sequence of mathematical statements $P(1),$ $P(2),$ $P(3),…,$ where\n\n- $P(1)$ is true (as well as $P(2),P(3),P(4),…,$ if required), and\n\n- $P(1),P(2),…,P(k)⇒P(k+1)$ for every $k\\in N.$\n\nThen, $P(n)$ is true for every $n\\in N.$\n\nIn this case, the general statement $P(n)$ we're required to prove is the following:\n\n$$\nP(n):\\,{a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n}\n$$\n\nWe start by proving the base cases. Since the first application of the recurrence formula ${a}_{n+1}=7{a}_{n}-10{a}_{n-1}$ does not apply until ${a}_{3},$ we must check the base cases $P(1)$ and $P(2).$\n\n**Base Cases**: We first prove our statement is true for the base cases $n=1,2.$ \nFor $n=1,$ for the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=3,\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{5}^{1}-{2}^{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for $n=2,$ for the left-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=21,\n$$\n\nand for the right-hand side, we have\n\n$$\n{5}^{2}-{2}^{2}=21.\n$$\n\nThus, our statement is true for $n=1$ and $n=2.$\n\nNext, we write down our (strong) **inductive hypothesis,** which is to assume that $P(n)$ is true *for all* $n\\le k,$ where $k\\ge 2.$\n\n**Inductive Hypothesis**: We assume that ${a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n}$ for all $n\\le k$ for some $k\\ge 2.$ In particular, we have the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{k} & ={5}^{k}-{2}^{k} \\\\ {a}_{k-1} & ={5}^{k-1}-{2}^{k-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must show that $P(1),P(2),…,P(k)⇒P(k+1).$ Let's start by writing down $P(k+1).$ This is the first part of the inductive step.\n\n**Inductive Step**: We're required to prove that\n\n$$\n{a}_{k+1}={5}^{k+1}-{2}^{k+1}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThe idea is to rewrite the left-hand side of $(∗)$ using the recurrence relation and inductive hypothesis to show that this equals the right-hand side. We do this as follows:\n\nUsing the recurrence relation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{k+1} & =7{a}_{k}-10{a}_{k-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the inductive hypothesis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}_{k}-10{a}_{k-1} & =7({5}^{k}-{2}^{k})-10({5}^{k-1}-{2}^{k-1}) \\\\  & =7({5}^{k})-7({2}^{k})-10({5}^{k-1})+10({2}^{k-1}) \\\\  & =7({5}^{k})-7({2}^{k})-2\\cdot 5({5}^{k-1})+5\\cdot 2({2}^{k-1}) \\\\  & =7({5}^{k})-7({2}^{k})-2({5}^{k})+5({2}^{k}) \\\\  & =5({5}^{k})-2({2}^{k}) \\\\  & ={5}^{k+1}-{2}^{k+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required.\n\nSince we've shown that the left-hand side of $(∗)$ equals the right-hand side, our proof is complete. So, let's write down our conclusion.\n\n**Conclusion**: Therefore, by the principle of strong induction, ${a}_{n}={5}^{n}-{2}^{n}$ is true for all $n\\in N.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fde4921b-bf5d-50a5-b94b-070b6de67fdb" "answer-field-55466cac-5f4e-53ff-ad9e-8548c1792814" "answer-field-0598fbab-c6cc-58d8-8ae5-6a424e8b4f8c" "answer-field-aa46c984-4456-5e1d-af70-5c1f2d6829f0" "answer-field-1e3afe87-357a-5078-953a-97ac295227a1" "answer-field-6425011c-7d1e-5d35-9111-6bc997246436" "answer-field-96754219-7475-5010-a30f-6e4e2c9776d5" "answer-field-3918b44c-9df1-54b2-9068-07cfde5329de" "answer-field-6d78aa45-8a7d-57ce-a944-a2bf94f4075e" "answer-field-0a9935fb-8204-53e3-9a19-c8167e551afe" "answer-field-1f490514-ea0c-5e7a-b061-3c5922a4b7ba" "answer-field-65db749b-199b-5804-adbd-e3b3a927e961" "answer-field-7d1355a7-7f7c-513e-bf20-fda46aca15df" "answer-field-d5f9f8d0-6553-58ba-98c8-5de231789f6f" "answer-field-478bc6f4-cff0-5543-baca-5b47cbbdfa92" "answer-field-e3e0ec6b-8e98-58a4-8359-d790349c320f" "answer-field-e2464548-add4-5ec5-9eab-86a52ef0ad9d" "answer-field-7e114eac-5cd1-5bcf-b3e2-103d5ca1ea04" "answer-field-dd64c3a5-ec6f-5d16-98d0-c28c407d0b68"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fde4921b-bf5d-50a5-b94b-070b6de67fdb" :answer-field/id #uuid "fde4921b-bf5d-50a5-b94b-070b6de67fdb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4ce6ec0c-c6e8-593c-b309-656b88de4872" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ce6ec0c-c6e8-593c-b309-656b88de4872" "answer-8853a4dd-a43b-58fe-af10-aaf0e1abc24b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ce6ec0c-c6e8-593c-b309-656b88de4872" :answer/id #uuid "4ce6ec0c-c6e8-593c-b309-656b88de4872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8853a4dd-a43b-58fe-af10-aaf0e1abc24b" :answer/id #uuid "8853a4dd-a43b-58fe-af10-aaf0e1abc24b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-55466cac-5f4e-